def sqrt_newton(n, tol=1e-9):
    if n < 0: raise ValueError('negative input')
    x = float(n)
    while True:
        x_new = 0.5 * (x + n / x)
        if abs(x_new - x) < tol:
            return x_new
        x = x_new

Convergence: quadratic — each iteration approximately doubles the number of correct digits. Starting from x₀ = n, converges in O(log(log(1/tol))) iterations to tolerance tol.
This is far faster than bisection's linear O(log(1/tol)) convergence.
